## 4. Selection and sizing

- Environmental exposure: dust, humidity, wash-down and mechanical contact along the cable route.
- Whether maintenance crews will re-train the cable, which argues for a thicker outer wall.
- Availability of spare parts, because a second outage on the same feeder is expensive.
- Insulation diameter and screen cut-back length as measured on the actual cable.
- Whether a partial discharge test is required at commissioning.

## 5. Standards commonly specified

- IEC 60502-4, test requirements for accessories for cables from 6 kV up to 30 kV.
- IEC 61442, test methods for accessories above 3.6 kV up to 36 kV.
- IEC 60664-1, insulation coordination.
- IEC 60502-1, the cable standard that fixes the insulation geometry and temperature basis.

Standards are listed as those normally cited for this component class. They describe the requirement, not a claim of certification. Test evidence applicable to a specific order is confirmed per purchase order.

## 6. Handling and installation

- Protect the opened cable ends from dust during the outage. In a mining environment this is the single largest source of contamination.
- Keep the recovered sleeve mechanically protected until the joint is closed and backfilled.
- Check the accessory against the cable insulation diameter before starting the cut-back.
- Record installation data for the maintenance file so the next crew does not have to re-derive it.

## 7. Failure modes and mitigation

| Failure mode | Likely cause | Mitigation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Partial discharge after installation | Contamination at the interface, or an installation error in the stress control region | Protect the interface from dust, follow the drawing, and test at commissioning where required. |
| Mechanical damage to the outer wall | Cable re-trained across an edge during maintenance | Respect the bend radius and protect the sleeve where the route is congested. |
| Long downtime on a repeat failure | No spare accessory held for the feeder | Hold one spare kit per critical feeder. |
| Moisture ingress | Sealing incomplete on a damp installation day | Dry the surfaces and apply the sealing system to drawing. |

## 8. Typical applications

- Mining distribution and heavy industrial substations.
- Industrial distribution where cable routes are congested and re-work is likely.
- MV cable OEMs supplying site-specific lengths with accessories.
- Utility and contractor maintenance where downtime cost dominates the accessory price.

